Z||000000||Monkeyman||10-18-2001||08:22 PM||||My new furnace is hooked up and working!!  We had some water damage about a month ago (4' of water in the basement).  It took out the furnace and the hot water heater.  Now we have a new hot water heater and a brand new furnace.  It's been getting a little chilly the past few nights (31* last night).  Now we have heat again.  Ahh!  What a feeling.  I never knew heat felt so good.  Our new furnace is much quieter than the old POS, too.  And it's amazing how much better (and faster) it heats up the house.<P>Time to quit rambling.  I had to tell somebody.  Who better to tell than you guys.<BR><P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||10
Z||000001||Mach10||10-18-2001||08:34 PM||||Monkey-man is back in his tropical environment, eh? You think YOU had it bad, you should check out the snow-baboons of Siberia  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000002||Monkeyman||10-18-2001||08:44 PM||||My cousins in Siberia have a little more hair than I do (although not much  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> ) so they tend to stay warmer.  The cold doesn't usually bother me, but after a while it just sinks into your bones.  And it doesn't help the arthritis in my back much.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif">  Maybe I can sleep more than 20 minutes at a time tonight.  Hopefully I'll be back to my 'normal' 3-4 hours.||||reg||1
